# Trivy vulnerability exemptions — SA4E-385 release gate (SEC-04).
# Standard .trivyignore format: one vulnerability ID per line.
# Each entry below is a release-accepted risk with a documented reason.
#
# NOTE: CVE-2026-126190 (soupsieve 2.10) is NOT exempted here. It is fixed by
# upgrading soupsieve to 4.0.1 in both MCP venvs (/opt/markitdown-venv and
# /opt/markdown-exporter-venv) in the Dockerfile mcp-python stage
# (ARG SOUPSIEVE_VERSION=4.0.1, --ignore-requires-python, importlib.metadata
# assertion + descendant-selector smoke test). Do NOT add CVE-2026-126190 to
# this file — if a post-fix Trivy scan still reports it, report it explicitly
# instead of silently exempting it.

# body-parser 2.3.0 — DoS via unhandled decompression stream error.
# Fixed in 2.4.0; locked resolution pending scheduled dependency bump (SA4E-385).
CVE-2026-111181

# undici 6.29.0 / 7.30.0 / 8.10.2 — DoS via unhandled stream error on excessive
# content-length. Transitive dependency of the pi-coding-agent stack.
CVE-2026-109869

# zod 3.25.76 — DoS via unbounded array validation.
# Fix requires zod v4 migration (breaking API change); tracked separately.
CVE-2023-54404

